o a necesidades distintas.\nQué se puede revisar: en los expedientes enlazados, qué se contrató en cada caso y en qué fechas, y si varios contratos atienden una misma necesidad que pudo contratarse de una vez.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 135 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 31.0 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 4.3, with a 95% confidence interval of 3.4 to 5.5. December accounts for 11% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 8% of all its services and supplies contracts. The contracts just under the limit are spread across 110 different awardees. Contract [1], for 14,500 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar trends could result from seasonal demand or budget cycles. The number of contracts does not prove misconduct, as market prices or budget constraints could explain the amounts near the limit.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and values of contracts awarded in December to see if they align with seasonal needs. Review the list of awardees to identify if multiple contracts were awarded to the same provider for similar services. Examine contract details to ensure no single provider was repeatedly awarded for the same purpose.","origen_es":"plantilla","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["3UhzpqRpHnOdkQsA7ROvsg%3D%3D","xioAH7M912HzAq95uGTrDQ%3D%3D","os%2FfWejKnXQadbH3CysQuQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}